## UI/UX Standards

- Prioritize accessibility and keyboard navigation.
- Maintain consistent spacing, typography, and visual hierarchy.
- Prefer responsive layouts by default.
- Avoid cluttered interfaces.
- Use loading, empty, and error states consistently.
- Preserve perceived performance with optimistic or streamed UI when appropriate.
- Use semantic HTML elements (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`).
- Ensure all interactive elements have accessible names (`aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`).
- Maintain keyboard navigability; visible focus states.
- Use `prefers-reduced-motion` media queries for animations.
- Run automated a11y checks via Playwright or axe-core in CI.
- Do not use `div` or `span` for clickable elements.

